## 3. scripts/ci/test-installer-bash-resolution.py (13 cases)

Generated executables per rule: exits non-zero, mimics the launcher's stdout-only
complaint, is a directory, a *working* bash under System32 that must still lose on
Windows (from both the `PATH` and the `$BASH` side), and must still win on POSIX.
Plus what check_install_sh reports when nothing is usable: a failure on POSIX, a note on
Windows, and the rest of the check still running when a bash is found.

